WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:07.007
"The Benefits of Quinine (Tonic Water)
to Suppress Hunger and Boost GLP-1"

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.510
Most of the poisons
used by humans

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:10.677
come from bitter plants.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:13.046
For example,
strychnine and hemlock.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.014
At the same time,

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.983
some of the most
popular beverages

00:00:15.983 --> 00:00:17.117
in the world are bitter,

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.786
as are some
of the healthiest foods.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:22.422
Bitter taste receptors
aren’t only on our tongue,

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.524
but throughout much
of our digestive tract,

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:27.527
on the very same cells
lining our gut that secrete

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:30.297
the appetite-suppressing
hormone, GLP-1.

00:00:30.297 --> 00:00:32.499
And indeed,
a number of bitter compounds

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.234
have been shown
to potently stimulate

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.103
the release of hormones
like GLP-1

00:00:36.103 --> 00:00:38.071
in Petri dishes and lab animals.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.007
What about people?

00:00:40.007 --> 00:00:41.341
And beer!

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.510
Beer is one of the most popular
bitter beverages,

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.546
thanks to hops.

00:00:45.546 --> 00:00:47.948
Given that bitter herbs
have evidently been used

00:00:47.948 --> 00:00:50.651
in times of scarcity
to reduce hunger,

00:00:50.651 --> 00:00:53.720
researchers tested low and high
doses of hops extracts

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.223
on people undergoing
a 24-hour fast,

00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:58.959
and found both doses seemed
to lower feelings of hunger

00:00:58.959 --> 00:01:00.460
better than placebo.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.629
Might that be a GLP-1 effect?

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:04.765
Let’s find out.

00:01:04.765 --> 00:01:07.367
Taking a hops extract
before a meal,

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.203
in either immediate
or delayed-release capsules,

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.506
led to significantly more
GLP-1 release

00:01:12.506 --> 00:01:14.174
than did a placebo.

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:15.509
And, more importantly,

00:01:15.509 --> 00:01:16.944
when the study participants
were given

00:01:16.944 --> 00:01:19.346
all-you-can-eat ham sandwiches
a few hours later,

00:01:19.346 --> 00:01:21.815
they ate significantly less.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.584
They didn’t feel significantly
less hungry or more full,

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:27.854
but, overall, still ate
about 200 calories less.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:29.990
So, a bitter hop extract

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:32.359
significantly decreased
calorie intake,

00:01:32.359 --> 00:01:34.428
while increasing
appetite-suppressing hormones,

00:01:34.428 --> 00:01:36.430
like GLP-1.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:38.632
These changes occurred
without the participants

00:01:38.632 --> 00:01:40.500
feeling any different,
appetite-wise,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.003
or liking the sandwiches
any less.

00:01:43.003 --> 00:01:45.539
Now, the extract
did make them feel

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:47.975
nauseated, bloat-y, and barf-y,

00:01:47.975 --> 00:01:49.576
but maybe
that’s just more evidence

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.078
it might be working
through GLP-1,

00:01:51.078 --> 00:01:52.412
since those are
common side effects

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:55.615
of the GLP-1-mimicking drugs,
like Ozempic.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.852
Well, wait,
no wonder they ate less,

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:01.755
but evidently, the degree
of gastrointestinal discomfort

00:02:01.755 --> 00:02:05.492
did not correlate
with how much less they ate.

00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:08.061
The main reason
I’d caution against hops

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.597
is because of a compound in hops
called 8-PN

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:11.965
that I’ve talked about before

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.067
in a two-part video series.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.137
What about quinine,

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.039
perhaps the best-studied
bitter substance

00:02:19.039 --> 00:02:20.440
in human history?

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.577
Extracted from the bark
of the cinchona tree,

00:02:23.577 --> 00:02:24.678
quinine was not only

00:02:24.678 --> 00:02:28.815
the first effective treatment
for malaria 400 years ago,

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.784
but, remarkably,
remains a common and effective

00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:32.619
treatment to this day.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:35.288
And give someone
275 milligrams of it,

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:38.191
and GLP-1 secretion
is stimulated.

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:41.028
Enough to actually reduce
appetite and body weight?

00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:44.431
"Dietary quinine reduces
body weight and food intake,"

00:02:44.431 --> 00:02:45.866
in rats.

00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:48.468
What about in people?

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.871
"Intragastric
quinine administration

00:02:50.871 --> 00:02:53.206
decreases hedonic eating,"

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:54.708
meaning eating for pleasure,

00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:56.276
even if you aren’t
really hungry.

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:58.445
In this case,
a chocolate milkshake.

00:02:58.445 --> 00:02:59.913
And if you’re thinking,
"Well, of course

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.448
they’d drink less milkshake

00:03:01.448 --> 00:03:04.217
if they just had something
super bitter," but, no.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.053
The quinine was administered

00:03:06.053 --> 00:03:08.055
directly into their stomach
through a tube,

00:03:08.055 --> 00:03:11.191
so it bypassed the bitter
receptors in their mouth.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.626
There are still
those bitter receptors

00:03:12.626 --> 00:03:13.627
in our gut, though,

00:03:13.627 --> 00:03:16.329
that we aren’t even
consciously aware of.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.198
The researchers
even did brain scans,

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.300
and concluded that
being unknowingly slipped

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.935
about 200 milligrams of quinine

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:24.271
not only affected
how much the study participants

00:03:24.271 --> 00:03:25.739
felt like they wanted to eat,

00:03:25.739 --> 00:03:27.507
but how much
they actually did eat,

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:30.677
by interfering
with reward brain circuits.

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:34.047
And you don’t have to go
lick some tree bark to get it.

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.083
It’s available
in every grocery store

00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:39.252
in the form of tonic water.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:42.656
A liter of tonic water has about
60 to 70 milligrams of quinine,

00:03:42.656 --> 00:03:45.559
and bitter lemon,
another popular cocktail mixer,

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:46.860
has about half that.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.829
But getting
200 milligrams of quinine

00:03:48.829 --> 00:03:52.132
still would be like drinking
three quarts of tonic water.

00:03:52.132 --> 00:03:53.900
Can we get away with less?

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.568
Yes.

00:03:54.568 --> 00:03:55.602
In this study, people were given

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:58.004
just 18 milligrams of quinine,
or placebo,

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.639
and then, an hour later,
everyone was given

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:01.908
all-you-can-eat
ham and cheese sandwiches.

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.544
And caloric intake
was significantly lower

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:07.514
after the quinine than placebo
by about 14 percent.

00:04:07.514 --> 00:04:11.051
So, drinking a third of a liter
of tonic water before a meal

00:04:11.051 --> 00:04:14.855
could reduce your caloric intake
by 82 calories.

00:04:14.855 --> 00:04:16.389
But a third of a liter
of tonic water

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.758
has more than
a hundred calories!

00:04:17.758 --> 00:04:20.494
So, that wouldn’t
do you much good.

00:04:20.494 --> 00:04:22.462
Tonic water is basically
quinine-spiked

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:24.564
carbonated sugar water.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.500
Now, there are
sugar-free varieties,

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.602
or, you could go
straight to the source.

00:04:28.602 --> 00:04:30.470
What if you got about
the same amount of quinine

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:33.073
in the form of powdered bark?

00:04:33.073 --> 00:04:35.108
The effects of giving about
a third of a teaspoon a day

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.409
of powdered cinchona bark

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:39.546
on satiety, weight loss,
and body composition

00:04:39.546 --> 00:04:41.948
in a population
of overweight adults.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.317
Significantly more weight loss,

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:47.420
significantly more waist lost,
and even slimmer hips

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.356
in the bark group,
compared to placebo,

00:04:49.356 --> 00:04:50.991
and the weight loss
was in fat mass,

00:04:50.991 --> 00:04:52.993
with greater
lean mass preservation,

00:04:52.993 --> 00:04:54.194
compared to placebo.

00:04:54.194 --> 00:04:55.929
So, in humans,

00:04:55.929 --> 00:04:57.998
quinine may boost GLP-1,

00:04:57.998 --> 00:04:59.966
decrease hedonic hunger,

00:04:59.966 --> 00:05:02.235
lower appetite,
decrease calorie intake,

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:04.371
and decrease body fat.

00:05:04.371 --> 00:05:06.106
What are the downsides?

00:05:06.106 --> 00:05:08.942
That’s what I’ll cover next.

